ttps://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app/commit/26b3c3b51d2bf68acb83ff49744ac4cab7ea2e4f","node_id":"C_kwDOG-yb0NoAKDI2YjNjM2I1MWQyYmY2OGFjYjgzZmY0OTc0NGFjNGNhYjdlYTJlNGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app/commit/d4f2e8313556832e2afa844e20074bc12184d4e2","sha":"d4f2e8313556832e2afa844e20074bc12184d4e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app/commits/d4f2e8313556832e2afa844e20074bc12184d4e2"}],"sha":"26b3c3b51d2bf68acb83ff49744ac4cab7ea2e4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app/commits/26b3c3b51d2bf68acb83ff49744ac4cab7ea2e4f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8509731?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/denniskigen","id":8509731,"login":"denniskigen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDk3MzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app/commits/d4f2e8313556832e2afa844e20074bc12184d4e2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T08:07:17Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"Dennis Kigen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T08:07:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(chore) Adopt @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9 (#883)\n\n* (chore) Adopt @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9\n\nLint config moves to a flat eslint.config.mjs that spreads\n@openmrs/eslint-config 2.0.0, replacing .eslintrc and .eslintignore. eslint\nmoves from 8.57 to ^9.39.0 and the --ext flag goes away, since flat config\nmakes it redundant.\n\nThis repo extends recommended-type-checked, so the type-aware preset is\nspread here too, with the same rules turned off that the previous config\nturned off, plus consistent-type-exports and unused-imports/no-unused-imports.\nComparing the effective rule sets before and after, nothing this repo\nenforced is lost.\n\nThe type-aware block is scoped to the files tsconfig.json actually covers:\nsrc, tools and vitest.config.ts. The old config asked for type information\nrepo-wide, which made every file under e2e a parse error, so e2e has never\nreally been linted. It is now, which is where most of the new reports come\nfrom.\n\nThose reports break down as follows. Five specs had a trailing top-level\ntest.afterEach, which now warns; a top-level hook applies to every test in\nthe file wherever it sits, so moving it above the tests changes nothing at\nruntime. Three waits use networkidle, and swapping those for a different\nwait is a behaviour change rather than a lint fix, so that rule is off for\ne2e with a note. The e2e override for react-hooks/rules-of-hooks is kept,\nsince Playwright fixtures take a callback named use and call it, and the\nfile-level directive in e2e/fixtures/api.ts is redundant alongside it.\n\nTwo component tests query through render''s container. Rewriting them to\nscreen queries is follow-up work, so those files disable the relevant\ntesting-library rules with that reason recorded, and the rules stay on\neverywhere else.\n\nFour unnecessary type assertions are removed. typescript-eslint moves from\n8.54 to 8.67 with the shared config, and the newer version reports them.\n\n* Keep ESLint config out of next updates\n\nReplace the @openmrs wildcard with the packages this repository actually tracks on the next tag. This prevents the stable-only ESLint config from breaking the scheduled dependency update workflow.","tree":{"sha":"0e797a66ea2188e7e9eddac0b151aee437dfa301","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app/git/trees/0e797a66ea2188e7e9eddac0b151aee437dfa301"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app/git/commits/d4f2e8313556832e2afa844e20074bc12184d4e2","verification":{"payload":"tree 0e797a66ea2188e7e9eddac0b151aee437dfa301\nparent 8b065d71b855ebbebcc7ff592f6e9245e1ad6173\nauthor Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com> 1786522037 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786522037 +0530\n\n(chore) Adopt @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9 (#883)\n\n* (chore) Adopt @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9\n\nLint config moves to a flat eslint.config.mjs that spreads\n@openmrs/eslint-config 2.0.0, replacing .eslintrc and .eslintignore. eslint\nmoves from 8.57 to ^9.39.0 and the --ext flag goes away, since flat config\nmakes it redundant.\n\nThis repo extends recommended-type-checked, so the type-aware preset is\nspread here too, with the same rules turned off that the previous config\nturned off, plus consistent-type-exports and unused-imports/no-unused-imports.\nComparing the effective rule sets before and after, nothing this repo\nenforced is lost.\n\nThe type-aware block is scoped to the files tsconfig.json actually covers:\nsrc, tools and vitest.config.ts. The old config asked for type information\nrepo-wide, which made every file under e2e a parse error, so e2e has never\nreally been linted. It is now, which is where most of the new reports come\nfrom.\n\nThose reports break down as follows. Five specs had a trailing top-level\ntest.afterEach, which now warns; a top-level hook applies to every test in\nthe file wherever it sits, so moving it above the tests changes nothing at\nruntime. Three waits use networkidle, and swapping those for a different\nwait is a behaviour change rather than a lint fix, so that rule is off for\ne2e with a note. The e2e override for react-hooks/rules-of-hooks is kept,\nsince Playwright fixtures take a callback named use and call it, and the\nfile-level directive in e2e/fixtures/api.ts is redundant alongside it.\n\nTwo component tests query through render''s container. Rewriting them to\nscreen queries is follow-up work, so those files disable the relevant\ntesting-library rules with that reason recorded, and the rules stay on\neverywhere else.\n\nFour unnecessary type assertions are removed. typescript-eslint moves from\n8.54 to 8.67 with the shared config, and the newer version reports them.\n\n* Keep ESLint config out of next updates\n\nReplace the @openmrs wildcard with the packages this repository actually tracks on the next tag. This prevents the stable-only ESLint config from breaking the scheduled dependency update workflow.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfCm1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAm6MQAJ/iAtU1dAaHqudKmZr0YKOq\nhdJqxAIZy92G3iTudpY7iyXeYif/0KLN3UgN9KRFRkVYmYvdOILNxHsNXPgh+Jpd\n+N2pv4HjvE3A/jtvooJBshDg8obpCtlwkrmG3zEXv/Ktp+NRtici0P9osqjWyEn9\nfvWocyUMzTi94fowMnjyLgEYy3ZD8c129nAb0f9k+kyAaiVsTWrjXXgACmARIe/d\nlIJcaQJ0xtidIEnWNrpKy4xwbMihEYBEwgA22125VXWevmceuZHk8t5yX8vh4Ga6\nuScBqRg15mQeduvDAkdcmpAOjLxWmVRXOvIrXngyadqgVFAVa4kI6eQViSKdDZ1z\nKQr1h5a2EKo9V2ljBvMGuwAS1/p72YQ8SiiCL7lLEOqPAtXjq6WkLZIoqLFfWYHs\nOf+cDz97nMCASoiadgLBb+tuUzFIzHl/NSw06KFKZIYP5QUG6tW3HfSe9712O1zm\nXF+DIDMUP/8U5ao3zV48BuIgxCLDo2faP1evxjn2ZNNpyxn6Nvkm9StapujXg5jD\n1WxWO4z6wob06E4ZyD3z2zdtuEWjlHdrcW5Rpmv4sGwJ0Anz3ogj2riFyW/Yi1yQ\nftS7u+Imm/OdwHMdpwbtM36o94ChOgmVNJxcJzTwOfiVVKhLPOfAjpfL+KmWzMvd\nuAeFc3BM9pMzvoYVNw6x\n=YkFO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-12T08:07:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubus