9864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app/commit/f60aa895d2acbc36866cd6c7d58b9edeffd78334","node_id":"C_kwDOG-yb0NoAKGY2MGFhODk1ZDJhY2JjMzY4NjZjZDZjN2Q1OGI5ZWRlZmZkNzgzMzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app/commit/f95cf7935383e67e6e7b513a4ea91ff609b7f064","sha":"f95cf7935383e67e6e7b513a4ea91ff609b7f064","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app/commits/f95cf7935383e67e6e7b513a4ea91ff609b7f064"}],"sha":"f60aa895d2acbc36866cd6c7d58b9edeffd78334","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app/commits/f60aa895d2acbc36866cd6c7d58b9edeffd78334"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34070216?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NethmiRodrigo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NethmiRodrigo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NethmiRodrigo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NethmiRodrigo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NethmiRodrigo","id":34070216,"login":"NethmiRodrigo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MDcwMjE2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NethmiRodrigo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NethmiRodrigo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NethmiRodrigo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NethmiRodrigo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NethmiRodrigo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NethmiRodrigo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app/commits/f95cf7935383e67e6e7b513a4ea91ff609b7f064/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-22T17:44:52Z","email":"nethmi@openmrs.org","name":"Nethmi Rodrigo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-22T17:44:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(fix) Refresh prescriptions table in place after dispensing (#859)\n\n* (fix) Refresh prescriptions table in place after dispense\n\nrevalidate() used the global `mutate` imported from `swr`, which is bound to\nSWR''s default cache. OpenMRS wraps every microfrontend in an `<SWRConfig>` with\na custom cache provider, so all `useSWR` data (including the prescriptions\ntable) lives in that provider''s cache. The global `mutate`''s key filter\ntherefore never matched anything and the table was never revalidated, so the\nstatus/last-dispenser only updated after switching tabs (which changes the SWR\nkey) or a manual refresh.\n\nPass the cache-bound `mutate` from `useSWRConfig()` into revalidate() so it\ntargets the provider''s cache. Updated all callers (dispense/close/pause forms,\nthe on-prescription-filled modal, and the delete handler in history-and-comments).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* (chore) Avoid swr/_internal deep-import for ScopedMutator\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"857658555603198358c897b8fc637910050723e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app/git/trees/857658555603198358c897b8fc637910050723e3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app/git/commits/f95cf7935383e67e6e7b513a4ea91ff609b7f064","verification":{"payload":"tree 857658555603198358c897b8fc637910050723e3\nparent fe7c772a1acca27598d23e39dbaa475271b9f18a\nauthor Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org> 1782150292 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782150292 +0530\n\n(fix) Refresh prescriptions table in place after dispensing (#859)\n\n* (fix) Refresh prescriptions table in place after dispense\n\nrevalidate() used the global `mutate` imported from `swr`, which is bound to\nSWR''s default cache. OpenMRS wraps every microfrontend in an `<SWRConfig>` with\na custom cache provider, so all `useSWR` data (including the prescriptions\ntable) lives in that provider''s cache. The global `mutate`''s key filter\ntherefore never matched anything and the table was never revalidated, so the\nstatus/last-dispenser only updated after switching tabs (which changes the SWR\nkey) or a manual refresh.\n\nPass the cache-bound `mutate` from `useSWRConfig()` into revalidate() so it\ntargets the provider''s cache. Updated all callers (dispense/close/pause forms,\nthe on-prescription-filled modal, and the delete handler in history-and-comments).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* (chore) Avoid swr/_internal deep-import for ScopedMutator\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOXSUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGnwQAEHnjbY2adxgMyR/meQCXm5X\nI3zBPHrWigvGfd/uemti+szt1365qyk0/a5J0+Vnzh7o/lMhkwT5eEHYh8DYzWpi\npOgfOBR4ORMl7+8I5oH+GWzCizVM1LXUFNTYiNxV2npB9f8iL2Hqe/laTK1U4Alt\nkDlp90z3aaMSMqDI9tvVP2219s/9sZ8nGxBt1PnR0565bZ5t3qUNlEeaftOtZZyt\nmmZdmDDobChGKKQr6cayNtAv0bv8+FCPNLjU1HNJB8YPJc3azI3tRYbvl4uyHGgn\nxreGOm33ZPS7ndpRdAqcpGK3VneFFoN5IIAJmRdZGbUI2UE0SaSF5kj74Ohbdq6n\nzr+hZXndCTvRDESm72Er8F3xb+ITpsIsjaYpXJXmvY8LXRLNuAb4gF6PCh4GGBan\naGod4yaxuSGAyUjYB8YRG6NDVqNQiwPsWgp1pljLszGHQms