:"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app/commits/120d22e968d57a1ce47a5a908e50e79f485cfcb1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-11T12:24:33Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"Dennis Kigen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-11T12:24:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(fix) Allow recording allergies from the fill prescription order basket (#854)\n\nThe allergy ''+'' control in the order basket''s drug search falls back to\nlaunching the patient chart''s allergy form workspace when the host does\nnot provide a launcher. The fill prescription workflow renders the order\nbasket outside the patient chart, so that fallback opened the\npatient-chart workspace group with null group props and crashed every\naction button registered to it with ''Cannot read properties of null\n(reading patientUuid)''.\n\nRegister the exported allergy form workspace from the allergies app into\nthe fill-prescription-window and pass its name as\nallergyFormWorkspaceName in the order basket window props, so the form\nopens as a child of the dispensing app''s own workspace window. This is\nthe same wiring the ward app added in\nopenmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management#2561 after the form was decoupled\nfrom the chart group in openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart#3353.","tree":{"sha":"5ba3fe08329d249b7630f3edf99bfd3a13e87cfb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app/git/trees/5ba3fe08329d249b7630f3edf99bfd3a13e87cfb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app/git/commits/120d22e968d57a1ce47a5a908e50e79f485cfcb1","verification":{"payload":"tree 5ba3fe08329d249b7630f3edf99bfd3a13e87cfb\nparent ac58e4729815cefdc87174c9ab9c2408a0121a1e\nauthor Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com> 1781180673 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781180673 +0530\n\n(fix) Allow recording allergies from the fill prescription order basket (#854)\n\nThe allergy ''+'' control in the order basket''s drug search falls back to\nlaunching the patient chart''s allergy form workspace when the host does\nnot provide a launcher. The fill prescription workflow renders the order\nbasket outside the patient chart, so that fallback opened the\npatient-chart workspace group with null group props and crashed every\naction button registered to it with ''Cannot read properties of null\n(reading patientUuid)''.\n\nRegister the exported allergy form workspace from the allergies app into\nthe fill-prescription-window and pass its name as\nallergyFormWorkspaceName in the order basket window props, so the form\nopens as a child of the dispensing app''s own workspace window. This is\nthe same wiring the ward app added in\nopenmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management#2561 after the form was decoupled\nfrom the chart group in openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart#3353.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKqkBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAouIQABcJ9/XjYQI7UIoxXt5X15HF\n3kM/k1sQS7juJsapDDpOjpuUvQKlh5MkuYt12F5admzzFuTUMBUd9/0OESujrtTk\nJDQBDc9ROm+Uc3rqzm2/JcjNdxuVc6qFQExufTG5lMPMMEGt6C5SnxEhqlscA6R3\nwlhJIatv1l5NB+TkRJStX9VZGTwCjHR5LD4oezLBSI2SA1vf/7c1exS/IxDpgOOf\nSmt9xHnIsDMh/WyeKurpw853RQ4EGFmZiN1qqWrKK5kv8PcJtzSo8l8Cvnr3Fanx\nl/fOYffAnFTGgmW+2L/V13hAzemWTIE7GKPiBI8NEr4H0agTchu9gbJA2Say+L8L\ntB4PWaOOjzxZLZeljpcuS9bYxhFL2yaFlkQUMFW2CoAF/8a2rYKF3aLJ1FT1f7KV\nFDE9UJklQAuiaiJIJvfD2jDdjz7qTDyRd3zftXX8kedm/tO6MltVkZwifC0O9o+J\nrpxZPK3fJajlHhD7bLeIh6Y8KbsitRCYRkOKj4PV8355jixfHHne8IDVZHfD0HTy\nRw8Gt