","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlashHand/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlashHand/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlashHand","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FlashHand/rig/commits/cc5e0a4cd01070dfc53b7d88bdd837f5c28d1f29/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-24T00:31:37Z","email":"ralwayne@163.com","name":"ral"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-24T00:31:37Z","email":"ralwayne@163.com","name":"ral"},"message":"feat(crew): pending-questions tracker per project\n\nAdds rig-agents/Projects/<project>/Pending-Questions.md scaffolded by\n`rig crew init` / `project add`, plus `rig crew pending {list|add|answer|remove}`\nto capture and resolve missing user-supplied materials (API keys, sample data,\nambiguous spec decisions, etc.) without breaking the agent loop.\n\n- list (default): cross-project open questions; --all to include resolved\n- add: records Q-YYMMDD-NNN with why / need / priority / asked-by, auto-detects\n  --project from CWD when run inside a registered project path\n- answer: moves Q to Resolved with --note as the recorded answer; preserves history\n- remove: hard delete (use answer to keep audit trail)\n\nVault agent block (CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md inside the vault) gets a new rule:\nagents must record blockers via `pending add` rather than silently asking, and\nself-resolve via `pending answer` once the human supplies the material.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dffebede1c0f9e94936cb14855cbdf0ff983434a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FlashHand/rig/git/trees/dffebede1c0f9e94936cb14855cbdf0ff983434a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FlashHand/rig/git/commits/cc5e0a4cd01070dfc53b7d88bdd837f5c28d1f29","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":