":"https://api.github.com/users/FlashHand/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlashHand/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlashHand/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlashHand","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FlashHand/rig/commits/34335c88edbfcbb46f4d186cb59883b780059591/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-23T17:40:51Z","email":"ralwayne@163.com","name":"ral"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-23T17:40:51Z","email":"ralwayne@163.com","name":"ral"},"message":"fix(publish): force --registry on CLI + scrub npm_config_* env from npm spawn\n\nyarn <script> injects `npm_config_registry=https://registry.yarnpkg.com`\ninto the child process env. That env wins over the `registry=...` line\nin our temp `.npmrc` (npm precedence: CLI flag > env > rc), so `yarn\ndeliver` was silently publishing — well, trying to publish — to\nyarnpkg.com instead of npmjs.org, which errors with `ENEEDAUTH ...\nhttps://registry.yarnpkg.com`.\n\n- Pass `--registry <REGISTRY>` explicitly on the CLI (strongest source).\n- Scrub `npm_config_*` env vars from the spawned child for belt-and-\n  braces; a stale `npm_config_registry` in any shell rc would otherwise\n  bite the same way outside yarn.","tree":{"sha":"dfc9c83eaa41e29b738b93c08803978534d7e38f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FlashHand/rig/git/trees/dfc9c83eaa41e29b738b93c08803978534d7e38f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FlashHand/rig/git/commits/34335c88edbfcbb46f4d186cb59883b780059591","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11323941?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlashHand/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlashHand/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlashHand/followin