"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cjmalloy/jasper-ui/commit/a23e1d0cbf1890bb327c3d0394dd20654b60e32d","node_id":"C_kwDOHBnFWtoAKGEyM2UxZDBjYmYxODkwYmIzMjdjM2QwMzk0ZGQyMDY1NGI2MGUzMmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cjmalloy/jasper-ui/commit/fcc88d51bf9a64e67998cd9f8f671d18732bdb2c","sha":"fcc88d51bf9a64e67998cd9f8f671d18732bdb2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cjmalloy/jasper-ui/commits/fcc88d51bf9a64e67998cd9f8f671d18732bdb2c"}],"sha":"a23e1d0cbf1890bb327c3d0394dd20654b60e32d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cjmalloy/jasper-ui/commits/a23e1d0cbf1890bb327c3d0394dd20654b60e32d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent","id":198982749,"login":"Copilot","node_id":"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cjmalloy/jasper-ui/commits/fcc88d51bf9a64e67998cd9f8f671d18732bdb2c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T05:04:46Z","email":"198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Copilot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T05:04:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Cross-origin account aliases and per-origin notification cursors (#1282)\n\n* Add cross-origin account alias mappings\n\n* Store notification cursors per origin\n\n* Complete per-origin notification cursor flow\n\n* Finalize notification paging and translations\n\n* Remove legacy lastNotified configuration\n\n* Inline notification cursor plugin tag\n\n* Potential fix for pull request finding\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Potential fix for pull request finding\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Bump user template version\n\n* Include alarm-only notification origins\n\n* Fix unread notification service mock\n\n* Cover remote alias notification flow\n\n* Clear notifications only for read origin\n\n* Await cursor writes before unread reload\n\n* Stop unread reload after destruction\n\n* Potential fix for pull request finding\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Use cached account aliases for lookup\n\n* Initialize cached aliases in account tests\n\n* Normalize local origin when clearing notifications and discover alarm origins lazily\n\nCo-authored-by: cjmalloy <1704049+cjmalloy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Count alarms from untracked origins and create their cursors when cleared\n\nCo-authored-by: cjmalloy <1704049+cjmalloy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Bound cursor loads, cancel superseded checks, discover alarm origins before clear-all, clear stream-less alarm origins, add aliases class\n\nCo-authored-by: cjmalloy <1704049+cjmalloy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Require local or two-sided declarations for account aliases\n\nCo-authored-by: cjmalloy <1704049+cjmalloy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add AccountService tests for paging, cursor writes, conflicts and cursor loading\n\nCo-authored-by: cjmalloy <1704049+cjmalloy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Refetch the cursor Ref and retry once on a cursor write conflict\n\nCo-authored-by: cjmalloy <1704049+cjmalloy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add OriginMapService alias tests for transitivity, url targets and missing origins\n\nCo-authored-by: cjmalloy <1704049+cjmalloy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Treat a Ref without an origin as local in isCurrentAccountRef\n\nCo-authored-by: cjmalloy <1704049+cjmalloy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Merge the cursor plugin into settings Refs that have no cursor yet\n\nCo-authored-by: cjmalloy <1704049+cjmalloy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Include account alias mailboxes in the inbox query\n\nCo-authored-by: cjmalloy <1704049+cjmalloy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Check that clearing @repl notifications keeps local ones in the outbox e2e\n\nCo-authored-by: cjmalloy <1704049+cjmalloy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add plugin-origin-aliases e2e sanity test\n\nCo-authored-by: cjmalloy <1704049+cjmalloy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Load saved alarm-origin cursors before falling back to the aggregate alarm query\n\nCo-authored-by: cjmalloy <1704049+cjmalloy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Change type from ''tags'' to ''users'' in origin.ts\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Ignore in-flight cursor loads and writes from a previous account\n\nCo-authored-by: cjmalloy <1704049+cjmalloy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Bound concurrency of notification count and page requests\n\nCo-authored-by: cjmalloy <1704049+cjmalloy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Refactor write handling in account service\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Map remote outbox origins to local aliases when displaying users\n\nCo-authored-by: cjmalloy <1704049+cjmalloy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Resolve nested remote origins through the replication chain instead of only API URLs\n\nCo-authored-by: cjmalloy <1704049+cjmalloy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Resolve remote origins by url + remote only, following our push/pull mirrors transitively\n\nCo-authored-by: cjmalloy <1704049+cjmalloy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add regression test for recipients of a comment mirrored through eggnog\n\nCo-authored-by: cjmalloy <1704049+cjmalloy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add test for city declaring its own url with a plain +plugin/origin Ref\n\nCo-authored-by: cjmalloy <1704049+cjmalloy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Ignore trailing slash when matching own API url\n\nCo-authored-by: cjmalloy <1704049+cjmalloy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Retry requests rejected for a missing CSRF token\n\nCo-authored-by: cjmalloy <1704049+cjmalloy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix cursor precision, alarm cursor fallback, push-only aliases and cursor plugin gating\n\nCo-authored-by: cjmalloy <1704049+cjmalloy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Chris Malloy <cjmalloy@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: cjmalloy <1704049+cjmalloy@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"cbe5edab39f771d064f1ebe8ecf4a05e0435dd42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cjmalloy/jasper-ui/git/trees/cbe5edab39f771d064f1ebe8ecf4a05e0435dd42"},"url":"https://api.github.com/r